Package: mlr3HTE
Title: Metalearner Learners for Heterogeneous Treatment Effects
Version: 0.41
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Flexible", family = "Pangzi", role = c("cre", "aut"),
           email = "zhangkaicr@foxmail.com")
Description: A small, mlr3-native R package that implements the S-, T-, X-, R-
    and DR-learners for conditional average treatment effect (CATE) estimation.
    The same engine covers continuous, binary and survival outcomes and handles
    both randomized (RCT) and observational data (via internal propensity-score
    IPTW or user-supplied weights). Survival outcomes are supported natively via
    'survival' and 'ranger' (no 'mlr3proba' dependency). It ships both a
    functional API and a parametric mlr3 Learner subclass that plugs into
    resample()/benchmark()/tune(), a simulation grid with known ground truth,
    and a DALEX-based toolkit for explaining the estimated CATE surface.
